  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 removes automatic market withdrawal for models above 5% (no sales stop, no time limit) and keeps per-model results to regulators and purchasers, protecting Northwind's Hearth 10. S3 sets a 36-month new-unit deadline and a 72-month retrofit, which exceeds the 12-month and 84-month acceptable bounds for new units, while the retrofit meets Northwind's 6-year red line. S5 keeps an 8-per-100k mandatory recall with no transition, which would bind Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, though remedies and sales suspension are left to the regulator."
